## Building Detection

Find all buildings. They appear as:
- Coded IDs: "B00A - Admin Building - 1924 - Brick" or "D01 - Demountable"
- Named buildings: "Building Name: Main Building" or building names as section headers
- If no coded IDs exist, generate sequential IDs (B001, B002...) and set `name` to the actual building name

Interior/Exterior sections within a building are NOT separate buildings.

## Format-Specific Building Detection
{% set _format = detected_format or format_name or "" %}
{% if _format == "pipe_table" %}
### Pipe-Table Format (Greencap / Clutch)
- Buildings appear as sections with pipe-delimited metadata rows
- Look for: | Building Name: | <value> | Number of Levels: | <value> |
- Each building section has its own risk assessment table
- Extract ONLY the building name VALUE — NOT the label cell or the entire pipe row
- If the header contains "| Building Name: | X |", extract "X" as the name
- Page ranges span from the building header to the next building header
{% elif _format == "standard" %}
### Standard DET Format
- Buildings appear as section headers with coded IDs
- Look for: ## B001 - Building Name - Year - Construction
- Room codes follow pattern B###-R#### (e.g., B009-R0001)
- Buildings may appear in a summary grid/table (e.g., pages 3-15)
- Each grid row = one building (B001, B002, etc.)
- "No Asbestos" buildings should still be listed with complexity="simple"
- ACM data appears on later pages, referenced by building ID
{% elif _format == "ara" %}
### ARA Text-Header Format
- Buildings appear as sections with text headers
- Look for: "Building Name: Main Building" or "Building Name:\n  Main Building"
- Each building section has its own risk assessment table
- Extract ONLY the building name from the header — NOT the entire table row
- Page ranges span from the building header to the next building header
{% else %}
### Unknown Format — Check All Patterns
- Look for coded building IDs (B001, D01, B00A) in section headers
- Look for "Building Name:" text headers followed by a building name
- Look for pipe-delimited metadata rows: | Building Name: | <value> |
- Look for summary grids/tables listing buildings with IDs and metadata
- If no coded IDs exist, generate sequential IDs (B001, B002...)
{% endif %}

### General Rules
- Do NOT return raw markdown table rows as building names or IDs
- building_id should be a short code (B001, B00A, D01) — NOT a full table row
- building name should be a short name — NOT a pipe-delimited row

## For Each Building Extract

- building_id: code (B00A, D01) or generated (B001)
- name: building name
- year: year built (integer or null)
- construction: construction type or null
- purpose: building purpose or null
- levels: number of levels or null
- page_start: first page with building data (from "--- Page N ---" markers)
- page_end: last page with building data
- complexity: "simple" (no ACM found, or <3 items) or "complex" (multiple rooms/items)
- rooms: list of rooms found (see schema below)
- acm_item_count_estimate: estimated ACM item count or null

## Room Schema

```json
{"room_id": "B001-R0001", "name": "Room Name", "area_m2": null, "page": null}
```

## Processing Groups

Group buildings by page proximity, targeting 3-5 pages per group:
```json
{"group_id": 1, "building_ids": ["B001"], "page_start": 1, "page_end": 4, "estimated_pages": 4}
```

